<h3>Supported keys and user actions</h3>
<ul class="keyboard-legend">
    <li>
        <span class="button-preview">
            <span class="key-button">Tab</span>
        </span>
        <span class="button-descr">
            Lets you focus the next splitter bar to enable the features below.
        </span>
    </li>
    <li>
        <span class="button-preview">
            <span class="key-button">Up</span>
        </span>
        <span class="button-descr">
            Moves up the splitter bar in a vertical Splitter.
        </span>
    </li>
    <li>
        <span class="button-preview">
            <span class="key-button">Down</span>
        </span>
        <span class="button-descr">
            Moves down a splitter bar in a vertical Splitter.
        </span>
    </li>
    <li>
        <span class="button-preview">
            <span class="key-button">Left</span>
        </span>
        <span class="button-descr">
            Moves left a splitter bar in a horizontal Splitter.
        </span>
    </li>
    <li>
        <span class="button-preview">
            <span class="key-button">Right</span>
        </span>
        <span class="button-descr">
            Moves right a splitter bar in a horizontal Splitter.
        </span>
    </li>
    <li>
        <span class="button-preview">
            <span class="key-button">Enter</span>
        </span>
        <span class="button-descr">
            Toggles the collapsed state of the nearest collapsible pane.
        </span>
    </li>
</ul>
<h3>Notes</h3>
<ul>
    <li>The splitter panes render a <code>tabIndex="0"</code> so they are focusable and the browser adds them to the "tab" sequence.</li>
    <li>Double-click on a splitter bar, or pressing <code>Enter</code> when it is focused, collapses the closest collapsible pane (usually the one before the bar). Clicking or tapping the directional arrows on the bar lets you choose which pane to collapse.</li>
</ul>
